  "notes": "The lane's counter-example, and the research states it as one: \"maximal vocal over minimal harmony\". Everything expensive in this model is in the melody block — \"Melisma is the parameter — very high note-density, long runs on every phrase end, a full falsetto register above the break\" — so `densityPerBar` is the highest in this batch, `register` reaches into falsetto, `endVariation` is on and `intervals.step` dominates because a run is stepwise. The harmony stays where the entry puts it: `i–VI` and `i–iv` 2-chord loops with m9/m11 pads, plus \"a genuine 4-chord option inherited from 90s R&B, which is what separates him from the rest of the lane\" — that is the third family. Tempo is the entry's read band (124–156, clap on beat 3), which is why `halfTime` is true. \"Hand-clap layering (two claps a 32nd apart) is a habit\" is `layerClapOffsetMs`. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are the swing amount, every drum probability and density, and the 808 slide figures — the entry gives grammar (\"dense swung 16th hats with triplet rolls\", \"a snare roll into the hook\", \"long-decay 808 with slides between roots, mixed loud\") and no numbers. The 32nd-apart clap is converted to milliseconds at the entry's own tempo band, which is this author's arithmetic rather than a stated figure. ⚠ `confidence` is medium, mirroring the entry. ⚠ `session.bpm.mode` is **INFERRED**: the number is not stated in the entry, and it is an authored centre of gravity inside the band the entry does state. ⚠ **`session.keys` is INFERRED.** The entry names no key centre; its Keys line states only \"Flat minor keys dominate.\", so these values and their weights are an authored reading of that constraint and not a sourced list.",
